[237.785423, "o", "        \"answer\": \"The warnings and precautions associated with lopinavir and ritonavir include: 1) Risk of serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions (potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events). 2) Toxicity in preterm neonates due to high ethanol and propylene glycol content in the oral solution, which can cause life-threatening cardiac toxicity (complete AV block, bradycardia, cardiomyopathy), lactic acidosis, acute renal failure, CNS depression, and respiratory complications. 3) Pancreatitis (including fatalities), particularly in patients with marked triglyceride elevations. 4) Hepatotoxicity (hepatic dysfunction, elevated transaminases, hepatic decompensation, and fatalities), especially in patients with underlying hepatitis B or C or cirrhosis. 5) QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes. 6) PR interval prolongation, which can cause second or third-degree AV block. 7) Diabetes mellitus, hyperglycemia, or diabetic ketoacidosis. 8) Immune reconstitution syndrome and autoimmune disorders. 9) Large elevations in"]
[237.870541, "i", " total cholesterol and triglycerides. 10) Fat redistribution and accumulation. 11) Increased bleeding in patients with hemophilia. 12) Potential development of HIV resistance or cross-resistance.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"These interactions may lead to: Clinically significant adverse reactions, potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events from greater exposures of concomitant medications.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Toxicity in Preterm Neonates\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Postmarketing life-threatening cases of cardiac toxicity (including complete AV block, bradycardia, and cardiomyopathy), lactic acidosis, acute renal failure, CNS depression and respiratory complications leading to death have been reported, predominantly in preterm neonates receiving lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Pancreatitis\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Pancreatitis has been observed in patients receiving lopinavir and ritonavir therapy, including those who developed marked triglyceride elevations.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0017\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"There have been postmarketing reports of hepatic dysfunction, including some fatalities.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0018\",\n                \"section\": \"5.5 QT Interval Prolongation\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Postmarketing cases of QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes have been reported although causality of lopinavir and ritonavir could not be established.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0019\",\n                \"section\": \"5.6 PR Interval Prolongation\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Lopinavir and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported.\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    },\n    {\n        \"qid\": \"fbab4114f66e2dda\",\n        \"status\": \"ANSWERED\",\n        \"answer\": \"The important warnings and precautions associated with Paxlovid are: 1) Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions: Initiation of Paxlovid (a strong CYP3A inhibitor) in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A, or vice versa, may increase plasma concentrations of those medications, potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events. The most commonly reported concomitant medications resulting in serious adverse reactions were calcineurin inhibitors (e.g., tacrolimus, cyclosporine), followed by calcium channel blockers. 2) Hypersensitivity Reactions: Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with Paxlovid. 3) Hepatotoxicity: Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir. 4) Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development: Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-4"]
[237.870573, "i", "8c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0013\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Initiation of PAXLOVID, which contains ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving PAXLOVID, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Hypersensitivity Reactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with PAXLOVID .\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    },\n    {\n        \"qid\": \"2d63e0a82215867f\",\n        \"status\": \"ANSWERED\",\n        \"answer\": \"The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include: 1) Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions: Initiation of Paxlovid (a strong CYP3A inhibitor) in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A, or vice versa, may increase plasma concentrations of those medications, potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events. The most commonly reported concomitant medications resulting in serious adverse reactions were calcineurin inhibitors (e.g., tacrolimus, cyclosporine), followed by calcium channel blockers. 2) Hypersensitivity Reactions: Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with Paxlovid. 3) Hepatotoxicity: Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir. 4) Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development: Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0013\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Initiation of PAXLOVID, which contains ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving PAXLOVID, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Hypersensitivity Reactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with PAXLOVID .\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0"]
[237.870595, "i", "015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": \"8a99d6d6-fd9e-45bb-b1bf-48c7f761232a\",\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    }\n]\n\noutput_data = {\"answers\": answers}\nwith open('/workspace/answers.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(output_data, f, indent=2)\nprint(\"Saved answers.json successfully!\")\nEOF\npython3 make_answers.py\n"]
